# MONITORS — authored judgements about OUR OWN COMPUTATION, rather than about code.
#
# A fourth category, and the file is what says so (`pystrider/library.py`). A monitor is not a pattern —
# `recognizes` must never offer one as an account of what a construct IS. It is not a bridge; it
# translates nothing. And it is not an operation: the planner must never propose it, because a monitor is
# not a way of getting anything done.
#
# ⭐ **That last one is STRUCTURAL rather than policed.** `driver.proposals` finds candidates through
# `function.producers`, which keys on the declared return type. A monitor declares none, so it produces
# nothing, so nothing can want it. The category is documentation of a fact, not the enforcement of one.
#
# **⭐⭐ WHY THIS IS AUTHORED TEXT AND NOT PYTHON.** ugm's `pursue` already takes a `decide` hook, and a
# budget check written in Python would be four lines. The whole point is that it would then be OURS —
# invisible to the system running it, unstateable by anyone who does not write Python, and unable to be
# reasoned about by anything else. `stop` as ordinary data on the watched node is the same decision the
# hook makes, expressed where every other decision in this system lives.
#
# **⚠ A MONITOR POLLS, AND THAT IS NOT A WART.** It has to loop, because the thing it watches advances
# between its own steps. ugm probed removing the looping instructions from the ISA and recommended
# against it (HANDOFF §6e), and this is the third of their three independent arguments: under that change
# a watcher could not be written as one microfunction at all.

# Watch a generation and stop it if planning outruns its budget.
#
# ⚠ It watches the PURSUIT, not the search, because the search DOES NOT EXIST YET when the watcher is
# scheduled — `driver.open_pursuit` mints it on the pursuit's first step. So the first thing the loop
# does is poll for it. A monitor that had to be handed its subject up front could only ever watch things
# that had already started, which is most of the way to a post-mortem.
#
# ⚠ `steps` and `done` are read off the live search node. Nothing here is instrumentation we added: the
# state of a running computation is data because ugm made it data, and this file is the consumer that
# proves the claim was worth something.
fn watch_generating(p, budget):
    .again:
    GET R(s) F(p) "search"
    JMPNOT R(s) ".again"
    ATTR R(over) R(s) "done"
    JMPIF R(over) ".end"
    ATTR R(n) R(s) "steps"
    ATTR R(b) F(budget) "value"
    LT R(ok) R(n) R(b)
    JMPIF R(ok) ".again"
    SET R(s) "stop" "REFUSE"
    SET R(s) "stop_why" "generating this app imagined more states than the budget allowed"
    .end:
